# Android fork — regenerable / heavy artifacts (kept out so the fork stays small).
# (No git repo is required here; this just documents what's safe to delete.)

# Node / Vite
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/

# Rust / Tauri
**/target/
# The generated Android project IS tracked: allowBackup=false, the release
# no-cleartext split and signing live in its hand-edited files, and a fresh
# `tauri android init` would silently drop them. Its own .gitignores skip build output.
jarvis-studio-gui/src-tauri/gen/schemas/
**/android/build/
**/android/.tauri/
**/.gradle/

# Local-only, never published: the Python reference spec (held a live Spotify token)
# and the graphify graph (absolute paths from the dev machine, ~50 MB).
reference/
graphify-out/

# Logs & local
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets — never commit keys / keystores
*.keystore
*.jks
**/app_secrets_local.*
keystore.properties
local.properties
.env
.env.*
*service-account*.json

# Build output — regenerate with `npm run android:build[:debug]`
*.apk
*.aab
